From 4f2b5fba5212a32c4e4a889492cc153e1220e619 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lazerg <lazerg2@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:34:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] cookie: check the proxy actually used for the localhost
 exception
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Curl_secure_context() only looked at CURLOPT_PROXY, so a proxy picked up
from the environment (http_proxy, all_proxy) still let a Secure cookie
for localhost be set and sent in clear through the proxy. Use the
transfer's used_proxy bit instead.

Follow-up to 9ce01c5fe2f976fa818985e616f305b97d6a9326 #23710

Reported-by: Jordan Fréry
Fixes #23928
Closes #23933

[Hades: backport to curl 8.23.0, adapted. Upstream changes the condition
inside Curl_secure_context() after the master-only cleanup d9ab46a
("cookie: cleanups and parse faster") gave it a length argument; 8.23.0
with curl-9918 still has the two-argument function and the IS_PROXIED()
macro. The same change is made here: the macro goes and the localhost
exception tests data->info.used_proxy, which 8.23.0 already sets in
lib/url.c for every transfer (SOCKS or HTTP proxy, from the options or
the environment) and resets in Curl_initinfo(). Upstream's test 382 is
not carried, as the image does not build curl's tests; it was run
against this backport.]

Upstream: https://github.com/curl/curl/commit/4f2b5fba5212a32c4e4a889492cc153e1220e619
---
 lib/cookie.c | 8 +-------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/cookie.c b/lib/cookie.c
index 183c0f5..4b9f96f 100644
--- a/lib/cookie.c
+++ b/lib/cookie.c
@@ -1290,16 +1290,10 @@ static int cookie_sort_ct(const void *p1, const void *p2)
   return (c2->creationtime > c1->creationtime) ? 1 : -1;
 }
 
-#ifdef CURL_DISABLE_PROXY
-#define IS_PROXIED(d) 0
-#else
-#define IS_PROXIED(d) !!CURL_EASY_STR(d, STRING_PROXY)
-#endif
-
 bool Curl_secure_context(struct Curl_easy *data, const char *host)
 {
   return Curl_xfer_is_secure(data) ||
-    (!IS_PROXIED(data) &&
+    (!data->info.used_proxy &&
      (curl_strequal("localhost", host) ||
       !strcmp(host, "127.0.0.1") ||
       !strcmp(host, "::1")));
